<title>USA: Marathon sets executive changes.</title>
<headline>Marathon sets executive changes.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>USX Corp said Wednesday that Jimmy Low would become assistant to the president of Marathon Oil Co and John Surma would succeed Low as senior vice president-finance &amp; accounting for Marathon, effective Febuary 1.</p>
<p>Surma comes to Marathon from the Pittsburgh office of Price Waterhouse LLP, where he is an audit partner.</p>
<p>Low has been in his current post with Marathon since 1989. He joined USX's former Oilwell Division in 1959 and moved through a series of supervisory posts in the accounting department before transferring to the U.S. Steel Group in 1974.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
